 "answer": "Yes. **The haze is bad in Kuala Lumpur today, Saturday, October 17.** At 11 a.m. local time, the reported Malaysian Air Pollutant Index (API) was **163 in Cheras** and **161 in Batu Muda**—both in the *unhealthy* range. Readings can change through the day. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nI’d skip strenuous outdoor exercise. If you need to be outside for a while, a well-fitting N95 can help reduce exposure; people with heart or lung conditions should be especially cautious. ([moh.gov.my](https://www.moh.gov.my/teras/info-kesihatan/jerebu/artikel-dan-panduan-pengguna-berkaitan-jerebu/health-advisory-for-workplaces-during-haze?utm_source=openai))",
